-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/800dabe8-201b-47e9-a66c-e4cfdd2f0fc6
-- title:
--   Conditional shrinking: a strict compression constant from a norm signal and a vanishing condition
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a unital C*-algebra with its usual order ($x\ge0$ means that $x$ is self-adjoint with spectrum in $[0,\infty)$). A *representation* of $A$ is a unital $*$-homomorphism $\pi:A\to B(H)$ into the bounded operators on a complex Hilbert space $H$. For $h\in A$ let
--   $$\operatorname{Her}(h)=\overline{\{\,h\,b\,h^*:\ b\in A\,\}}$$
--   be the closed subalgebra generated by the sandwiches $hbh^*$ (the hereditary subalgebra of $h$ when $h\ge0$). For $p,q,c\in A$ and $\kappa\in\mathbb{R}$ say that $c$ is *$\kappa$-compressed between $p$ and $q$* if $\|x\,c\,k\|\le\kappa\,\|x\|\,\|k\|$ for all $x\in\operatorname{Her}(p)$ and all $k\in\operatorname{Her}(q)$.
--
--   Let $a,y,c,p\in A$ with $a\ge0$, $y\ge0$, $p\ge0$, $\|p\|\le1$, $\|y\|\le1$, $\|c\|\le1$ and $p\in\operatorname{Her}(a)$, and put $d=y\,(1-c^*p^2c)\,y$. Assume:
--
--   1. for every representation $\pi$ of $A$ with $\|\pi(a)\|>\tfrac12$ one has $\|\pi(p)\|=1$;
--   2. for every representation $\pi$ of $A$ with $\pi(d)=0$ one has $\|\pi(y)\|\le\tfrac14$.
--
--   Then there exist $p_1,q_1\in A$ and $\kappa\in\mathbb{R}$ such that
--   $$0\le p_1,\quad \|p_1\|\le1,\quad p_1\in\operatorname{Her}(a),\qquad 0\le q_1,\quad \|q_1\|\le1,\quad q_1\in\operatorname{Her}(y),\qquad 0\le\kappa<1,$$
--   $$\|x\,c\,k\|\le\kappa\,\|x\|\,\|k\|\qquad\text{for all }x\in\operatorname{Her}(p_1),\ k\in\operatorname{Her}(q_1),$$
--   and such that for every representation $\pi$ of $A$: if $\|\pi(a)\|>\tfrac12$ then $\|\pi(p_1)\|=1$, and if $\|\pi(y)\|>\tfrac12$ then $\|\pi(q_1)\|=1$.
--
--   The theorem turns information about $p$ that is available one representation at a time into a uniform norm inequality: $c$ becomes strictly contractive (with constant $\kappa<1$) between a hereditary subalgebra under $a$ and one under $y$, while the norm signals (full norm of $p_1$ and $q_1$ in every representation where $a$, respectively $y$, has norm above $\tfrac12$) are preserved. Combined with a construction of a suitable $p$ from proper infiniteness, it gives the unital shrinking lemma used in the diagonalization argument.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Representations are the elements of `HilbertRep.{u,u} A`: a Hilbert space in the same universe as $A$ together with a unital star-algebra homomorphism from $A$ to its bounded operators. The order on $A$ is `CStarAlgebra.spectralOrder`; $\operatorname{Her}(h)$ is `Her h` and the compression condition is `HerCompression p₁ q₁ c κ`. The hypothesis $a\ge0$ is part of the statement but is not used in the proof.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/CStarAlgebra/PureInfiniteness/Shrinking.lean#L21-L84

